        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-31T01:56:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems like it will be very useful information if we ever use frame times as feedback to optimize the selected frequency.\n\nHowever, isn\u0027t this a property of a particular app/process? What happens if there are multiple apps contributing to the experience. Eg, a split screen where appA is targeting 30fps and appB is targeting 60fps?\n\nIf an app notifies the HAL of a 60fps rate and then the top-app is switched to another app that doesn\u0027t know about this hint, is the HAL notified that the period is now \"unknown\"?\n\nWhen the app is switched back, is the 60fps rate sent to the HAL again?",
      "revId": "371c6fe57763a0aabb15b5ba3b16e37ff5542f96",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
