        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-31T01:56:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What are the units of this hint? Does the picard framework convert this into an absolute load value (eg, 0-1023 scale usable to program uclamp values)? The app hint API appears to expose a delta (\u003e1.0 to indicate increase and \u003c1.0 to indicate decrease). Who keeps track of the current load that the delta applies to?\n\nAgain, what happens if that app is no longer top-app, does the HAL get notified? Is it reapplied when the app becomes top-app again?\n\nDo actions like this map better onto task profiles than HAL hints?",
      "revId": "371c6fe57763a0aabb15b5ba3b16e37ff5542f96",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
